$ ----------------------------------------------------------------------
$ Small stationary SWAN smoke test
$ Domain: 2 km x 1 km, constant depth, waves and wind from the west
$ ----------------------------------------------------------------------

PROJECT 'QUICK' '001'
SET NAUTICAL
MODE STATIONARY TWODIMENSIONAL
COORDINATES CARTESIAN

$ Computational grid: 20 x 10 meshes (21 x 11 points).
$ Spectral grid: 24 directions and 16 frequencies from 0.05 to 1.0 Hz.
CGRID REGULAR 0.0 0.0 0.0 2000.0 1000.0 20 10 CIRCLE 24 0.05 1.0 16

$ A 2 x 2 input grid is sufficient for the spatially constant 20 m depth.
INPGRID BOTTOM REGULAR 0.0 0.0 0.0 1 1 2000.0 1000.0
READINP BOTTOM 1.0 'bottom.bot' 3 0 FREE

$ Uniform 8 m/s wind and a 1 m, 6 s JONSWAP spectrum enter from the west.
WIND 8.0 270.0
BOUND SHAPESPEC JONSWAP 3.3 PEAK DSPR DEGREES
BOUNDSPEC SIDE WEST CONSTANT PAR 1.0 6.0 270.0 20.0

$ Keep the physics explicit so changes to defaults do not alter the smoke test.
GEN3 KOMEN
BREAKING CONSTANT 1.0 0.73
FRICTION JONSWAP CONSTANT 0.038

$ A compact full-grid map plus an easy-to-inspect value at the domain centre.
BLOCK 'COMPGRID' NOHEADER 'quick_test_hs.blk' LAYOUT 3 HSIGN
POINTS 'CENTER' 1000.0 500.0
TABLE 'CENTER' HEADER 'quick_test_center.tbl' XP YP DEPTH HSIGN TM01 DIR

COMPUTE
STOP
